IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ofek-domain`

§ `The 2025-2026 wage reduction`

-- ===========================================================================
-- HOW A WAR REACHES A PAYSLIP.
--
-- As part of the 2025 State budget the Knesset enacted, in Chapter 9 of the
-- Budget Objectives Act 5785-2025 (published 27 March 2025), a temporary
-- provision titled "Law for the participation of employees and office-holders
-- in the public service in steps for fiscal stabilisation during 2025 and
-- 2026". Its mechanism is unusual and is the reason this module exists:
--
--   the Act does NOT itself set the reduction for a group that reaches an
--   agreement. It reduces pay "in accordance with the provisions laid down in
--   a collective agreement applying to the employee, APPROVED for this
--   purpose by the Minister of Finance or the Wage Commissioner"; and only in
--   the ABSENCE of such an approved agreement does the Act's own § 3 rate
--   apply.
--
-- For teachers on Ofek Hadash terms that approved agreement is the collective
-- agreement of 29 June 2026 between the State and the Teachers' Union, and it
-- is the operative instrument. Everything below is from that agreement unless
-- the Act is named.
--
-- WHY THE ACT IS NOT ENCODED FROM ITS OWN TEXT. The corpus's copy of the Act
-- is a PDF extraction of the whole Budget Act, and the corpus itself records
-- that PDF-extracted text is bidi-damaged: in Chapter 9 the Hebrew arrives
-- with words duplicated and reversed, so that the definition of "the
-- determining base" appears twice, interleaved with itself. The collective
-- agreement's copy of the SAME definition is clean, and it is the instrument
-- that governs here in any event. NOTES.md § 5 records this as a deliberate
-- choice about which of two sources to encode from, not an oversight.
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Sections 6 and 7 — who is caught`

-- § 6 catches state employees of the Ministry of Education graded in the
-- teaching grade and employed on Ofek Hadash terms, including in ulpanim, and
-- teaching staff in instruction roles for the instruction fraction of their
-- post. § 7 excludes two groups "for the avoidance of doubt".
DECLARE `a place of employment for the 2026 agreement` IS ONE OF
    `an education institution on Ofek Hadash terms`   -- § 6
    `an ulpan on Ofek Hadash terms`                   -- § 6
    `an instruction role on Ofek Hadash terms`        -- § 6
    `a teacher training college`                      -- § 7, excluded
    `a supervision or headquarters role`              -- § 7, excluded

GIVEN `the place` IS A `a place of employment for the 2026 agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2026 agreement applies to work` `the place` IF
    CONSIDER `the place`
    WHEN `an education institution on Ofek Hadash terms` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an ulpan on Ofek Hadash terms`                 THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an instruction role on Ofek Hadash terms`      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a teacher training college`                    THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a supervision or headquarters role`            THEN FALSE

§§ `Section 8 — the determining base`

-- § 8 defines "the determining base" (ha-basis ha-kove'a) as SALARY, less
-- four things. The exclusions are what make the reduction narrower than it
-- looks: the two annual allowances that a teacher would most notice — the
-- recreation payment and the clothing allowance — are outside the base, and
-- are dealt with separately and once by § 20.
DECLARE `a component of the pay packet` IS ONE OF
    `a payment made monthly weekly or daily`                       -- inside the base
    `a payment neither periodic nor computed on other components`  -- § 8(a), out
    `the recreation payment`                                       -- § 8(b), out
    `the clothing allowance`                                       -- § 8(b), out
    `a reimbursement of expenses`                                  -- § 8(c), out
    `an employer grossing-up of the employee's tax`                -- § 8(d), out

GIVEN `the component` IS A `a component of the pay packet`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the component is in the determining base` `the component` IF
    CONSIDER `the component`
    WHEN `a payment made monthly weekly or daily`                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a payment neither periodic nor computed on other components` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the recreation payment`                                      THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the clothing allowance`                                      THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a reimbursement of expenses`                                 THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an employer grossing-up of the employee's tax`               THEN FALSE

§§ `Section 9 — the rates, and the two periods`

`the first day of the first reduction period` MEANS YMD 2025 5 1
`the last day of the first reduction period` MEANS YMD 2025 12 31
`the first day of the second reduction period` MEANS YMD 2026 1 1
`the last day of the second reduction period` MEANS YMD 2026 12 31

`the rate for the first reduction period` MEANS 0.95%   -- § 9(a)
`the rate for the second reduction period` MEANS 1.2%   -- § 9(b)

GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reduction rate on` `the date`
    @nlg the wage reduction rate applying on %the date%
    MEANS
    -- § 9(a): 1.5.2025 to 31.12.2025 — 0.95% of the determining base.
    -- § 9(b): 1.1.2026 to 31.12.2026 — 1.2%. Outside those two windows the
    -- temporary provision does not bite at all: it is an hora'at sha'a, and
    -- it expires.
    BRANCH IF `the date` `is before` `the first day of the first reduction period` THEN 0
           IF `the date` AT MOST `the last day of the first reduction period` THEN `the rate for the first reduction period`
           IF `the date` AT MOST `the last day of the second reduction period` THEN `the rate for the second reduction period`
           OTHERWISE                                                                    0

GIVEN `the determining base` IS A NUMBER
      `the date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the monthly wage reduction on` `the determining base` `the date`
    @nlg the monthly wage reduction on a determining base of %the determining base%
    MEANS `the determining base` TIMES (`the reduction rate on` `the date`)

-- § 12: the base on which the employer's study-fund contribution is computed
-- is reduced by the same rate, so the reduction reaches beyond take-home pay
-- into the teacher's savings.
GIVEN `the study fund base` IS A NUMBER
      `the date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the study fund base after the reduction` `the study fund base` `the date`
    @nlg the study fund base after the section 12 reduction
    MEANS `the study fund base` TIMES (1 MINUS (`the reduction rate on` `the date`))

§§ `Section 18 — what the reduction is NOT allowed to touch`

-- § 18 is the article that keeps a temporary cash saving from becoming a
-- permanent cut to a pension. Five payments are computed "as they would have
-- been calculated but for these provisions, that is, as though they had been
-- paid at their time and without the reduction".
DECLARE `a payment computed on salary` IS ONE OF
    `a one-off payment on the end of employment`      -- § 18(1)
    `an employer contribution to a pension fund`      -- § 18(2)
    `the determining salary for a budgetary pension`  -- § 18(3)
    `a payment of budgetary pension`                  -- § 18(4)
    `a bridging payment or purchased pension top-up`  -- § 18(5)
    `ordinary monthly pay`                            -- not listed: reduced

GIVEN `the payment` IS A `a payment computed on salary`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reduction is ignored in computing` `the payment` IF
    CONSIDER `the payment`
    WHEN `a one-off payment on the end of employment`     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an employer contribution to a pension fund`     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the determining salary for a budgetary pension` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a payment of budgetary pension`                 THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a bridging payment or purchased pension top-up` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `ordinary monthly pay`                           THEN FALSE

§§ `Sections 15 and 16 — the seniority step, given and taken back`

-- § 15 says the rules for recognising seniority for advancement in the salary
-- table are unchanged. § 16 then says, "notwithstanding § 15 and any other
-- agreement", that a teacher entitled to a seniority advancement in the
-- September 2025 salary shall have their pay reduced BY THE AMOUNT OF THE
-- INCREASE, in the salaries from September to December 2025 inclusive.
--
-- So the step is recognised — the teacher's place in the table really does
-- move, and stays moved — and its cash value is withheld for four months.
-- This is a distinct reduction from § 9, and it stacks on top of it.
`the first month the seniority step is withheld` MEANS YMD 2025 9 1
`the last month the seniority step is withheld` MEANS YMD 2025 12 31

GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seniority step is withheld on` `the date` IF
        NOT (`the date` `is before` `the first month the seniority step is withheld`)
    AND `the date` AT MOST `the last month the seniority step is withheld`

GIVEN `the value of the seniority step` IS A NUMBER
      `the teacher advanced in seniority in september 2025` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 16 withholding on` `the value of the seniority step` `the teacher advanced in seniority in september 2025` `the date`
    @nlg the section 16 withholding of a seniority step worth %the value of the seniority step%
    MEANS
    IF `the teacher advanced in seniority in september 2025` AND (`the seniority step is withheld on` `the date`)
        THEN `the value of the seniority step`
        ELSE 0

§§ `Section 20 — the clothing allowance, reduced once`

-- § 20 takes back, from the 5785 (2024/25) clothing allowance alone, the sum
-- of two things: the whole of that year's index-linkage, and a flat 91
-- shekels. § 20(b) is careful to add that the following year's allowance is
-- computed as though this had not happened — so this is a one-off, and it
-- does not compound.
`the flat part of the clothing allowance reduction` MEANS 91   -- § 20(a)(1)(b)

GIVEN `the allowance with index linkage` IS A NUMBER
      `the allowance without index linkage` IS A NUMBER
      `the fraction of a full post` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the clothing allowance reduction for 2025` `the allowance with index linkage` `the allowance without index linkage` `the fraction of a full post`
    @nlg the one-off 2025 clothing allowance reduction
    MEANS
    -- § 20(a)(2): a teacher on a part post, or employed for part of the
    -- school year, bears the proportionate part.
    (      (`the allowance with index linkage` MINUS `the allowance without index linkage`)
     PLUS  `the flat part of the clothing allowance reduction`)
    TIMES `the fraction of a full post`

§§ `Sections 24 and 25 — the extra substitution hour`

-- A curiosity, and the encoding's clearest single example of why a corpus has
-- to be read rather than assumed. In the 5786 school year teachers perform ONE
-- additional frontal substitution hour, on top of the hours in their post, and
-- § 25 prices it at 25% of the value of an hour.
--
-- 25%, not 125%. Every other hour worked on top of a post in this scheme is
-- paid at 125% (2008 §§ 29, 30) or at 100% (2008 § 33(c)(3)). The corpus
-- records that this figure was checked against the signed scan precisely
-- because it reads like a typo, and it is not one: the agreement calls it a
-- special rate for this agreement, lower than the ordinary substitution rate.
-- It is a concession extracted in exchange for the industrial peace § 29 buys.
`the rate for the section 25 additional hour` MEANS 25%
`the additional hours required in the 5786 school year` MEANS 1

-- § 26: §§ 24 and 25 do not reach a teacher who did regular work on 4 May
-- 2025 according to their fixed timetable — the day of the industrial action
-- the agreement is settling.
GIVEN `the teacher worked normally on 4 May 2025` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the additional hour is required of the teacher` IF
    NOT `the teacher worked normally on 4 May 2025`

GIVEN `the value of an hour` IS A NUMBER
      `the teacher worked normally on 4 May 2025` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the pay for the section 25 additional hour` `the value of an hour` `the teacher worked normally on 4 May 2025`
    @nlg the pay for the additional substitution hour under section 25
    MEANS
    IF `the additional hour is required of the teacher` `the teacher worked normally on 4 May 2025`
        THEN `the value of an hour` TIMES `the rate for the section 25 additional hour`
        ELSE 0

§§ `Section 17 — one line on the payslip`

-- § 17 requires the whole of the §§ 9 to 16 reductions to appear as a SINGLE
-- line, named "Economic Arrangements Law — Ofek". Encoded because it is the
-- only thing in this agreement a teacher actually sees, and because it means
-- the § 9 reduction and the § 16 withholding are not separately visible to
-- the person they are taken from.
`the name of the line on the payslip` MEANS "חוק הת. כלכלית אופק"

GIVEN `the determining base` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the seniority step` IS A NUMBER
      `the teacher advanced in seniority in september 2025` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the single payslip line for` `the determining base` `the value of the seniority step` `the teacher advanced in seniority in september 2025` `the date`
    @nlg the total shown on the single payslip line required by section 17
    MEANS   `the monthly wage reduction on` `the determining base` `the date`
      PLUS  `the section 16 withholding on` `the value of the seniority step` `the teacher advanced in seniority in september 2025` `the date`

§§ `Illustrations`

`a day in november 2025` MEANS YMD 2025 11 1
`a day in march 2026` MEANS YMD 2026 3 1
`a day in march 2027` MEANS YMD 2027 3 1
`a day in april 2025` MEANS YMD 2025 4 1

-- § 9: the two rates, and the two boundaries of the temporary provision.
#ASSERT `the reduction rate on` `a day in april 2025` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the reduction rate on` `a day in november 2025` EQUALS 0.95%
#ASSERT `the reduction rate on` `a day in march 2026` EQUALS 1.2%
#ASSERT `the reduction rate on` `a day in march 2027` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the reduction rate on` (YMD 2025 5 1) EQUALS 0.95%
#ASSERT `the reduction rate on` (YMD 2025 12 31) EQUALS 0.95%
#ASSERT `the reduction rate on` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS 1.2%
#ASSERT `the reduction rate on` (YMD 2026 12 31) EQUALS 1.2%
#ASSERT `the reduction rate on` (YMD 2027 1 1) EQUALS 0

-- On a determining base of 12,000 the reduction is 114 a month in 2025 and
-- 144 a month in 2026.
#ASSERT `the monthly wage reduction on` 12_000 `a day in november 2025` EQUALS 114
#ASSERT `the monthly wage reduction on` 12_000 `a day in march 2026` EQUALS 144

-- § 8: the recreation payment and the clothing allowance are OUTSIDE the
-- base, so the percentage reduction never touches them. § 20 is how the
-- clothing allowance is reached instead, once.
#ASSERT NOT `the component is in the determining base` `the recreation payment`
#ASSERT NOT `the component is in the determining base` `the clothing allowance`
#ASSERT NOT `the component is in the determining base` `a reimbursement of expenses`
#ASSERT `the component is in the determining base` `a payment made monthly weekly or daily`

-- § 18: the reduction is ignored for everything that determines a pension,
-- and applies to ordinary monthly pay.
#ASSERT `the reduction is ignored in computing` `an employer contribution to a pension fund`
#ASSERT `the reduction is ignored in computing` `the determining salary for a budgetary pension`
#ASSERT `the reduction is ignored in computing` `a one-off payment on the end of employment`
#ASSERT NOT `the reduction is ignored in computing` `ordinary monthly pay`

-- § 12: the study fund base falls by the same rate.
#ASSERT `the study fund base after the reduction` 10_000 `a day in march 2026` EQUALS 9_880

-- § 16: a seniority step worth 130 a month is withheld from September to
-- December 2025 and not afterwards — and it STACKS on the § 9 reduction, so
-- a teacher who advanced loses 114 plus 130 in November 2025.
#ASSERT `the section 16 withholding on` 130 TRUE `a day in november 2025` EQUALS 130
#ASSERT `the section 16 withholding on` 130 TRUE (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the section 16 withholding on` 130 FALSE `a day in november 2025` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the single payslip line for` 12_000 130 TRUE `a day in november 2025` EQUALS 244
#ASSERT `the single payslip line for` 12_000 130 FALSE `a day in november 2025` EQUALS 114
#ASSERT `the single payslip line for` 12_000 130 TRUE `a day in march 2026` EQUALS 144

-- § 20: a full-post teacher whose indexed allowance is 2,500 against 2,400
-- unindexed gives up 100 of linkage plus the flat 91.
#ASSERT `the clothing allowance reduction for 2025` 2_500 2_400 1 EQUALS 191
#ASSERT `the clothing allowance reduction for 2025` 2_500 2_400 (50%) EQUALS 95.5

-- §§ 24-26: the additional hour, at a quarter of the value of an hour, and
-- not required of a teacher who worked normally on 4 May 2025.
#ASSERT `the pay for the section 25 additional hour` 64.15 FALSE EQUALS 16.0375
#ASSERT `the pay for the section 25 additional hour` 64.15 TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the additional hour is required of the teacher` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the additional hour is required of the teacher` TRUE

-- The rate really is a quarter, and it is the only rate in this encoding
-- BELOW the value of the hour it pays for.
#ASSERT `the rate for the section 25 additional hour` EQUALS 25%

-- §§ 6-7: who is caught, and the two groups expressly outside.
#ASSERT `the 2026 agreement applies to work` `an education institution on Ofek Hadash terms`
#ASSERT `the 2026 agreement applies to work` `an ulpan on Ofek Hadash terms`
#ASSERT NOT `the 2026 agreement applies to work` `a teacher training college`
#ASSERT NOT `the 2026 agreement applies to work` `a supervision or headquarters role`
